//! The ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 module, Espressif, with the PCB antenna: the U1 of the Easyduino
//! ESP32-S3 board.
//!
//! The pin table was WRITTEN BY HAND from Espressif's datasheet "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 &
//! ESP32-S3-WROOM-1U Datasheet", Version 1.8 (revision history dated 2026-03-02, 53 pages,
//! fetched on 2026-11-10 from
//! <https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32-s3-wroom-1_wroom-1u_datasheet_en.pdf>):
//! Figure 3-1 "Pin Layout (Top View)" (printed page 10) for the pad numbers and Table 3-1 "Pin
//! Definitions" (printed pages 11 and 12) for the names and the types (P power, I input, I/O/T
//! input, output and high impedance). The datasheet is copyrighted (Espressif Systems
//! (Shanghai) Co., Ltd., all rights reserved): only facts are taken here (numbers, names,
//! kinds), none of its text or table.
//!
//! The datasheet says the module has 41 pins: the 40 edge pads and `EPAD`, the ground pad at
//! the middle of the underside. Pad 41 is one pin here, as the datasheet has it; the footprint
//! draws it as the nine 0.9 mm squares of the recommended land pattern, all numbered 41, as
//! Easyduino's board does. Pads 1 and 40 are ground too.
//!
//! The names are the datasheet's (`IO4`, `RXD0`, `TXD0`). Which pad is which GPIO of the chip
//! is in Table 3-1's function column: the pad `RXD0` is GPIO44 (U0RXD), `TXD0` is GPIO43
//! (U0TXD), `IO19` is GPIO19 and `USB_D-`, `IO20` is GPIO20 and `USB_D+`. The strapping pins
//! (Table 4-1, printed page 13) are GPIO0 (pad `IO0`, weak pull-up), GPIO3 (`IO3`, floating),
//! GPIO45 (`IO45`, weak pull-down) and GPIO46 (`IO46`, weak pull-down).
//!
//! The supply is a rail, `.vdd` (the `3V3` pad and the ground pads), with the datasheet's
//! recommended window: Table 6-2 (printed page 27) VDD33 3.0 V minimum, 3.3 V typical, 3.6 V
//! maximum, so the DC analysis checks a regulator's output against it. The table's other row,
//! "current delivered by external power supply" 0.5 A minimum, is a requirement on the supply and
//! not a draw: the module's own current is not stated (the datasheet's power consumption figures
//! are typical values for the radio's states, none was read), and a board states what its
//! regulator supplies.
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the alternate functions of the pads (Table 3-1's last
//! column: touch, ADC, SPI, UART, JTAG, clock outputs), the levels, ratings and timing (the
//! part is a boundary of the design: the checks that need a number are listed as not
//! evaluated), and the other variants' differences (footnote b of Table 3-1: with Octal SPI
//! PSRAM the pads `IO35`, `IO36` and `IO37` are not available; footnote c: on the ESP32-S3R16V
//! `IO47` and `IO48` work at 1.8 V). The catalog row is the N4 variant (4 MB quad flash, no
//! PSRAM), where all of them are available.

import std::sources::Rail

/// The ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 module: a Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE module with a PCB antenna, 18 x 25.5
/// mm, 40 edge pads and a ground pad, on 1.27 mm pitch. The pad numbers are the datasheet's.
/// `.vdd` is its supply, the rail of the `3V3` pad and the ground pads.
part Esp32S3Wroom1 {
    .designator &= "U"

    .vdd: Rail
    // Table 6-2, Recommended Operating Conditions (printed page 27): VDD33 3.0 V to 3.6 V.
    .vdd.voltage >= 3.0V
    .vdd.voltage <= 3.6V

    pins "SMD, 25.5x18mm" {
        //  pin     kind           name     pads
        .vdd.neg power        "GND"    "1" "40" "41"
        .vdd.pos power        "3V3"    "2"
        .en     input         "EN"     "3"
        .io4    bidirectional "IO4"    "4"
        .io5    bidirectional "IO5"    "5"
        .io6    bidirectional "IO6"    "6"
        .io7    bidirectional "IO7"    "7"
        .io15   bidirectional "IO15"   "8"
        .io16   bidirectional "IO16"   "9"
        .io17   bidirectional "IO17"   "10"
        .io18   bidirectional "IO18"   "11"
        .io8    bidirectional "IO8"    "12"
        .io19   bidirectional "IO19"   "13"
        .io20   bidirectional "IO20"   "14"
        .io3    bidirectional "IO3"    "15"
        .io46   bidirectional "IO46"   "16"
        .io9    bidirectional "IO9"    "17"
        .io10   bidirectional "IO10"   "18"
        .io11   bidirectional "IO11"   "19"
        .io12   bidirectional "IO12"   "20"
        .io13   bidirectional "IO13"   "21"
        .io14   bidirectional "IO14"   "22"
        .io21   bidirectional "IO21"   "23"
        .io47   bidirectional "IO47"   "24"
        .io48   bidirectional "IO48"   "25"
        .io45   bidirectional "IO45"   "26"
        .io0    bidirectional "IO0"    "27"
        .io35   bidirectional "IO35"   "28"
        .io36   bidirectional "IO36"   "29"
        .io37   bidirectional "IO37"   "30"
        .io38   bidirectional "IO38"   "31"
        .io39   bidirectional "IO39"   "32"
        .io40   bidirectional "IO40"   "33"
        .io41   bidirectional "IO41"   "34"
        .io42   bidirectional "IO42"   "35"
        .rxd0   bidirectional "RXD0"   "36"
        .txd0   bidirectional "TXD0"   "37"
        .io2    bidirectional "IO2"    "38"
        .io1    bidirectional "IO1"    "39"
    }

    .mpn: String
    .package: Package
    catalog esp32_s3_wroom_1 by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
